menu "Tab5 screen"

config TAB5_DIM_SECONDS
    int "Dim the screen after this many idle seconds"
    default 60
    range 5 3600

config TAB5_OFF_SECONDS
    int "Turn the backlight off after this many idle seconds"
    default 180
    range 10 86400
    help
        Idle means no touch and no motion from the IMU. Music keeps playing;
        state polling pauses while the backlight is off.

config TAB5_DIM_PERCENT
    int "Dimmed brightness percent"
    default 15
    range 1 100

endmenu

menu "Tab5 bring-up diagnostics"

config TAB5_I2C_SCAN
    bool "Run an I2C bus scan instead of starting the UI"
    default n
    help
        Enumerates every address on the BSP I2C bus under the same power
        sequence the display driver uses, then returns without initializing
        the panel. Used to identify the touch controller on hardware whose
        revision the board support package does not recognise.

        When enabled the device never starts the LVGL UI, so nothing appears
        on screen and the serial log is the only output.

config TAB5_FORGET_SPEAKERS
    bool "Forget stored speaker addresses at every boot"
    default n
    help
        Erases the manual speaker IP and the saved room IPs on each boot,
        so the controller must find a speaker through SSDP discovery.
        Wi-Fi credentials and saved areas are kept. Used to test discovery
        on hardware; flash the normal build afterwards.

endmenu
